Generally wizards have to get their artifact weapons by sacrificing, as 
they need the skills opened up too (there are conditions under which you 
can open up a skill through being crowned, but that's a bit too 
complicated IMO.) An exception would be the Staff of Aesculapius for 
neutral wizards, but this is a two-handed weapon so not necessarily 
recommended.

You already had to wish twice for the MKoT, so more artifact wishes 
would have been a bad idea anyway.

After reconsidering, I agree with the other posters that a +6/7 
Magicbane makes sense for wizards, since it's easily available and they 
won't really be relying on it anyway. Starting a sacfest just to get a 
better weapon doesn't really make sense for them.


